# Run targeted tests, not the whole suite

After each step, run only the tests for the files or feature you created or changed. Do not run the full suite unless the user asks.

Activate Node first for Nest services (see `node-version.mdc`).

## NestJS (`api-gateway`, `worker-node`)

- Changed `src/modules/<feature>/...`: that feature's unit specs and its e2e spec.
- Changed shared `src/common/...`, `src/config/...`: also specs of importers (`rg -l "<file-stem>" src test`).
- Changed Prisma/SQL migrations under `infrastructure/` or the service: e2e for the owning module.
- New test files: run them.

```bash
cd services/api-gateway && source ~/.nvm/nvm.sh && nvm use 24.22.2 && \
npx vitest run src/modules/attendance && \
npm run test:e2e -- attendance
```

## FastAPI (`vision-engine`)

```bash
cd services/vision-engine && \
python -m pytest tests/test_<module>.py -q
```

## Other checks

- Lint only changed files (Nest: `npx oxlint` / `eslint` as configured; Python: `ruff` / `mypy` if present).
- Keep cheap project checks the plan lists (`npm run build`, compose config validate); they are not test suites.

## Reporting

Say which tests you ran and that the full suite was not run, e.g. "Ran attendance unit (12) and e2e (4) tests; full suite not run."
